
# Student Management ER Diagram

This diagram represents the relationship between Students,
Courses, and Enrollments.

```mermaid
erDiagram
    STUDENTS ||--o{ ENROLLMENTS : registers
    COURSES ||--o{ ENROLLMENTS : includes

    STUDENTS {
        int student_id PK
        varchar first_name
        varchar last_name
        varchar email
        varchar phone
        date date_of_birth
    }

    COURSES {
        int course_id PK
        varchar course_name
        varchar course_code
        int credits
    }

    ENROLLMENTS {
        int enrollment_id PK
        int student_id FK
        int course_id FK
        date enrollment_date
        varchar grade
    }
```

## Relationships

- One student can enroll in multiple courses.
- One course can have multiple students.
- Enrollments connects Students and Courses.
- PK means Primary Key.
- FK means Foreign Key.
